  "_about": "The formats of the invocation bench (docs/invocacao-design.md, section 3): the same thing, of another matter. Each is a drawing on the grid, as a recipe of the game is, read anywhere on the grid and mirrored. 'M' (or the key 'principal' names) is the principal part, the matter of the thing: any matter fills it, and every square of it must hold the same. The other keys are the parts that stay what they are (an item, or '#' and a tag). A grid that the game's own recipe makes is that recipe's thing; only a grid no recipe makes is a format's conjured thing. 'damage' and 'speed' are what the thing has made of iron (the bonus to the hand, as the game's sword of iron has 5); other matter weighs more or less than iron and hits as much more or less.",
